response:
 If yes, then provide its prime factorization.
Here's a program that determines a prime factorization of any integer greater than one.
int isPrime(int num)
{
    if (num < 2) return 0;
    for (int i = 2; i <= num; i++)
        if (num % i == 0)
            return 0;
    return 1;
}

